# A copy per instance at 4 levels: each copy a class of one instance with no
# ready pass, whose registers and inputs hold over its stages, so only the
# values its logic computes cross stage registers (under a thousand
# bits, against over five thousand for the 4-instance copy, S4).
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/x1 --static --bubbles --copies Leaf:4 --stage-levels 4 Leaf > %t/x1.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=STABLE < %t/x1.log
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/x1/obj %S/Inputs/tb_late.sv top.sv %t/x1/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/x1/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/x1/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+12 +bubble=30 +stall=20 | FileCheck %s
# STABLE: Leaf staged: 14 stages, soonest {{[0-9]+}} stage register bits, latest {{[0-9][0-9]?[0-9]?}} (latest)
# Per class (--stage-levels-class): Leaf at 4 over a global 6 (14 stages, as
# at 4; against the target), Leaf off (unstaged), Leaf at 6 alone (as at 6),
# and a spec that matches no class.
