# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/zl/obj %S/Inputs/tb_late.sv top.sv %t/zl/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/zl/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/zl/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+9 +bubble=30 +stall=20 | FileCheck %s
# Unstaged, the leaf's cone is one host cycle of 49 estimated levels; at 6 and
# 4 levels a stage (counted as the logic screen does: a 12-bit compare or adder
# a LUT and a carry block, two chained choices a LUT), it spans 9 and 14 stage
# registers and no end point is much deeper than a stage. Of the cut soonest
# and the cut latest, the one of fewer stage register bits (STAGEBITS).
# PLAIN: Leaf x4 state gap {{[0-9]+}}{{$}}
# DEEP: #1 levels 49:
# S6: Leaf x4 state gap 4 stages 9
# S6: Leaf staged: 9 stages, soonest {{[0-9]+}} stage register bits, latest {{[0-9]+}} (latest)
# CUT6: #1 levels {{[4-7]}}:
# S4: Leaf x4 state gap 4 stages 14
# S4: Leaf staged: 14 stages, soonest {{[0-9]+}} stage register bits, latest {{[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]+}} (latest)
# CUT4: #1 levels {{[3-6]}}:
# CHECK: {{^}}MATCH 196 cycles
